)\n\nHOW IT WORKS:\nEach LoRA's activation delta is injected AT FORWARD TIME only into the\nimage tokens inside its bounding box. The LoRA physically cannot act\noutside its assigned region — it's a hard mask, not a soft nudge.\n\nHOW TO USE:\n  1. Node 4  — optional: load a global bypass/style LoRA here (or set\n               strength to 0 to skip it entirely).\n  2. Node 5  — Prompt Builder: describe your scene, then draw one\n               bounding box per character IN ORDER (left to right).\n               Each box should cover roughly where that person's face\n               will land in the final image.\n  3. Node 6  — Regional Multi-LoRA: one row per character. Use '+ Add\n               Region' to add more. Set each row to the LoRA for that\n               character. Order must match the boxes in Node 5.\n  4. Queue.\n\nREQUIRED MODELS:\n  UNet  : krea2_turbo_bf16.safetensors  (or krea2_bf16.safetensors)\n  CLIP  : qwen3vl_4b_bf16.safetensors\n  VAE   : qwen_image_vae.safetensors\n  (All available from the Krea 2 model release)\n\nKEY SETTINGS (Node 6):\n  split_mode     bbox = use drawn boxes (default, recommended)\n  seam_feather   0.08 = slight edge softening (raise to blur seams)\n  blend_override 0    = clean hard split (keep at 0)\n  bias_scale     ignored in this version (legacy, leave as-is)\n\nIf you leave split_mode on auto_vertical/auto_horizontal the canvas\nwill be divided into equal strips — no boxes needed."],"color":"#444","bgcolor":"#222"},{"id":60,"type":"EmptyLatentImage","pos":[-382.28084762163974,-631.1646188538218],"size":[318.7447265625,106],"flags":{},"order":5,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"宽度","name":"width","type":"INT","widget":{"name":"width"},"link":11},{"localized_name":"高度","name":"height","type":"INT","widget":{"name":"height"},"link":12},{"localized_name":"批量大小","name":"batch_size","type":"INT","widget":{"name":"batch_size"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"Latent","name":"LATENT","type":"LATENT","links":